 "about": "Beech above all, with sessile oak, hornbeam, ash, field maple and lime low down, pedunculate oak in the valleys and hedges, downy oak on warm limestone slopes and sweet chestnut on the acid soils of the Massif Central and the Rhine slopes; Norway spruce plantations on every upland, silver fir in the Jura, the Bavarian Forest and Auvergne, Scots pine on sand and poor rock, larch, Douglas fir and black pine planted; birch and rowan in the clearings, alder, willows and poplar rows along the rivers; hawthorn, blackthorn, hazel and dog rose in the hedges, broom on the acid hills, purging broom on the Auvergne heaths, juniper on the limestone grassland, mountain pine above the trees on the Krkonoše; bilberry, ferns, bracken and heather in the woods and heaths, purple moor-grass on the high bogs, reed in the fens; red pied Simmental and Montbéliarde cattle, black-and-white dairy cattle, white Charolais, brown Salers, Aubrac, Limousin and Brown Swiss, sheep flocks on the Alb, the Rhön and the causses, and horses; plastered houses with steep tile roofs, chalet-like farmhouses in Switzerland; hawthorn stands in for the apple, pear and cherry orchards.",
